Materialfy is based on spotifast (crmne, MIT) and yamusic-md3 (yaskorinov, MIT). Their copyright notices and
the MIT License text are kept in LICENSES/MIT.txt; authorship and what came from where are listed below.

1. spotifast (crmne) - Spotify logic
   https://github.com/crmne/spotifast
   Copyright (c) 2026 Carmine Paolino. MIT License.
   Taken from it: OAuth PKCE sign-in, Web API client, playback through librespot, Spotify Connect,
   queue, library, radio (crates/sf-auth, crates/sf-api, crates/sf-player, crates/sf-services).

2. yamusic-md3 (yaskorinov) - interface
   https://github.com/yaskorinov/yamusic-md3
   Copyright (c) 2025-2026 yaskorinov and contributors. MIT License.
   Taken from it: the QML interface and the Material 3 Expressive component library (src/materialfy/qml),
   the cxx-qt shell (crates/materialfy), cover-based theming (crates/mf-theme),
   lyrics (crates/mf-lyrics), platform services (crates/mf-platform),
   build and packaging scripts.

Third-party components
----------------------

- librespot (fork https://github.com/fatyzzz/librespot, based on crmne's patches) - MIT,
  Copyright (c) 2015 Paul Lietar and librespot-org contributors. Playback and Spotify Connect.
  The audio, connect, core, metadata and playback crates of that fork are copied into vendor/ (same
  revision, MIT license files kept), with one change in core: on Android it reports itself as Linux.
- fastframe-audio, fastframe-now-playing (https://github.com/dennisgr7/fastframe) - MIT,
  Copyright (c) 2026 Carmine Paolino. Audio output device, media keys and SMTC/MPRIS.
- hyper-proxy2 (fork https://github.com/crmne/hyper-proxy2) - MIT.
- cxx-qt (https://github.com/KDAB/cxx-qt) - MIT or Apache-2.0.
- Qt 6 (https://www.qt.io) - LGPL-3.0; the Qt libraries are linked dynamically and shipped
  unmodified; their sources are available at https://download.qt.io.
- Google Sans - SIL Open Font License 1.1 (src/materialfy/assets/fonts/LICENSE-GoogleSans.txt).
- Material Symbols Rounded - Apache License 2.0 (src/materialfy/assets/fonts/LICENSE-MaterialSymbols.txt).
- Other Rust dependencies - under the licenses stated in their packages (cargo metadata / Cargo.lock).

